    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Greeting people",
     "texto": [
      "**Bonjour** is the usual greeting during the day, in both formal and informal situations. In the evening, **bonsoir** is usually used.",
      "**Salut** is informal; it works for both greeting and saying goodbye. To say goodbye in a formal situation, use **au revoir**.",
      "In French it is polite to add **madame** or **monsieur**: **Bonjour, madame**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Tu and vous",
     "texto": [
      "**Tu** means «you» (informal): it is used with friends, family and children. **Vous** means formal «you» and also plural «you». With an adult you don't know, **vous** is a polite and safe choice; customs can vary depending on the relationship and the context.",
      "To say your name: **Je m'appelle Léa** (my name is Léa).",
      "To ask it: **Comment tu t'appelles ?** (informal) or **Comment vous vous appelez ?** (formal).",
      "Writing tip: in French, you leave a space before **?** and **!**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
